            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0084" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.0513/180: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-27T13:00:00+02:00">November 27, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 27—11:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>67. Legation’s telegram No. 65. I would appreciate some indication from the
                    Department as to when reply may be forthcoming as it is desirable, now that I am
                    again in Egypt, for me to be able to give the Egyptian authorities some
                    assurances on the subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
